-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 18, OFFENCES RELATING TO DOCUMENTS OR
-- ELECTRONIC RECORDS, FALSE INSTRUMENTS, AND TO CURRENCY AND BANK NOTES:
-- the "Forgery" part, ss 463-477A. (Currency and bank notes, ss 489A-489I,
-- are in pc-documents-defamation-currency.l4. There are no sections 478-489.)
--
--   s 463   defines "forgery"                    `commits forgery`
--   s 464   "making a false document"            `makes a false document or false electronic record`
--   s 465   punishes forgery
--   s 466   forgery of a court record, public register, power of attorney ...
--   s 467   forgery of a valuable security, will ...
--   s 468   forgery for the purpose of cheating
--   s 469   forgery for the purpose of harming reputation
--   s 470   "a forged document"                  (definition; no charge)
--   s 471   using as genuine a forged document
--   s 472, 473  counterfeit seal, plate or other instrument
--   s 473A, 473B, 473C  equipment for making a false instrument; "prejudice"
--   s 474   possessing a forged document of a s 466 or s 467 description
--   s 475, 476  counterfeit authenticating device or mark
--   s 477   fraudulent cancellation, destruction, etc., of a will
--   s 477A  falsification of accounts
--
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO "Current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026" (inputs/PC1871.txt), page footers removed.
--
-- Before reading:
--
-- * FAMILIES. One facts record per family (notes/PLAN.md §3.1):
--     `Forgery Facts`                   ss 463-470 (the forger's own acts)
--     `Forged Document Facts`           ss 471, 474 (using or holding a forged document)
--     `Counterfeit Seal Facts`          ss 472, 473
--     `False Instrument Equipment Facts` ss 473A, 473B (with `Prejudice Facts` for s 473C)
--     `Counterfeit Mark Facts`          ss 475, 476
--     `Will or Security Destruction Facts` s 477
--     `Falsification of Accounts Facts` s 477A
-- * s 463 reads s 464 as ONE call (`makes a false document or false
--   electronic record` f), drawn as one box with its own ladder stacked below
--   - the charge generator's `definitionFns`.
-- * "dishonestly" (s 24) and "fraudulently" (s 25) are flat leaves; their
--   Chapter 2 ladders are the drill-downs (DEFINITION_LADDERS).
-- * s 468 reads "cheating" (s 415), owned by pc-property. It is an INTENTION
--   here ("intending that the document ... shall be used for the purpose of
--   cheating"), so it is a leaf and needs no call into s 415 even at
--   integration; the @desc names the join anyway.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`
IMPORT `pc-documents-defamation-common`

§ `Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 18, forgery (ss 463-477A)`

§§ `The facts of one forgery - ss 463-469`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 463-469 - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC ss 124-125 require
DECLARE `Forgery Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the document`        IS A STRING  @desc The false document or electronic record, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "a medical certificate dated 3 March 2020 purporting to be issued by Dr Tan Ah Kow"
    `the manner`          IS A STRING  @desc How the accused made it false, as it is to read after the document - for example "by signing the name of Dr Tan Ah Kow on it without his authority"

    -- what the thing is: s 29 "document", s 29B "electronic record"
    `a document`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a document (s 29 - writing, a map, a photograph, a label, a disc or other device, marks with a meaning)?
    `an electronic record`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing an electronic record within the Electronic Transactions Act 2010 (s 29B)?

    -- s 464(1): "dishonestly or fraudulently"
    dishonestly           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act dishonestly - intending a wrongful gain or a wrongful loss, or in a way reasonable and honest people would call dishonest, knowing that (s 24)? (Fault element.)
    fraudulently          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act fraudulently - with intent to deceive, and by the deception to bring an advantage to anyone or a detriment to anyone else (s 25)? (Fault element.)

    -- s 464(1)(a)(i)-(iv): the acts
    `makes, signs, seals or executes a document or part of a document`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a)(i) Did the accused make, sign, seal or execute a document or part of one? Filling in a blank on a signed document is making part of it (s 464 illus (c), (d)). A man's signature of his own name may amount to this (Explanation 1).
    `makes any electronic record or part of any electronic record`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a)(ii) Did the accused make an electronic record or part of one?
    `affixes any electronic signature on any electronic record`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a)(iii) Did the accused affix an electronic signature (s 464(2): as in the Electronic Transactions Act 2010) on an electronic record?
    `makes any mark denoting the execution of a document or the authenticity of the electronic signature`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a)(iv) Did the accused make a mark denoting the execution of a document or the authenticity of an electronic signature?
    -- s 464(1)(a): the intention
    `intending it to be believed that it was made by or by the authority of a person by whom or by whose authority he knows it was not made`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Did the accused intend it to be believed that the document, record, part or signature was made, signed, sealed, executed or affixed by (or by the authority of) someone who, as he knew, did not make it or authorise it? The "someone" may be a fictitious person believed real, or a dead person believed to have made it in his lifetime (Explanation 2); it may bear the accused's own name, meant to pass as another's (Explanation 1). (Fault element.)
    `intending it to be believed that it was made at a time at which he knows it was not made`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Did the accused intend it to be believed that it was made, signed, sealed, executed or affixed at a time at which, as he knew, it was not - for example by antedating it (s 464 illus (h); Explanation 1 illus (d), (e))? (Fault element.)

    -- s 464(1)(b): alteration
    `without lawful authority`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Did the accused act without lawful authority?
    `alters a document or an electronic record in any material part after it has been made or executed`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Did the accused, by cancellation or otherwise, alter a document or electronic record in a material part, after it had been made, executed or affixed with an electronic signature (by himself or by anyone else, living or dead)?

    -- s 464(1)(c): causing another to sign
    `causes any person to sign, seal, execute or alter a document or an electronic record, or to affix his electronic signature`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Did the accused cause someone to sign, seal, execute or alter a document or electronic record, or to affix his electronic signature on an electronic record?
    `knowing that such person by reason of unsoundness of mind or intoxication cannot know the contents or the nature of the alteration`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Did the accused know that the person, because of unsoundness of mind or intoxication, could not know the contents of the document or record or the nature of the alteration? (Fault element.)
    `knowing that such person by reason of deception practised upon him does not know the contents or the nature of the alteration`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Did the accused know that the person, because of a deception practised on him, did not know the contents of the document or record or the nature of the alteration? (Fault element.)

    -- s 463: the intents
    `with intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make it intending to cause damage or injury (s 44) to the public (s 12) or to any person? (Fault element.)
    `with intent to support any claim or title`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make it intending to support any claim or title?
    `with intent to cause any person to part with property`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make it intending to cause anyone to part with property (s 22)?
    `with intent to cause any person to enter into any express or implied contract`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make it intending to cause anyone to enter into an express or implied contract - for example of employment (s 464 illus (k))? (FORK DD-2)
    `with intent to commit fraud or that fraud may be committed`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make it intending to commit fraud, or that fraud may be committed?

    -- s 466: what the forged thing purports to be
    `purports to be a record or proceeding of or before a court of justice`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 466: Does it purport to be a record or proceeding of or before a court of justice (s 20)?
    `purports to be a register of birth, baptism, marriage or burial`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 466: Does it purport to be a register of birth, baptism, marriage or burial?
    `purports to be a register kept by a public servant as such`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 466: Does it purport to be a register kept by a public servant (s 21) as such?
    `purports to be a certificate or document made by a public servant in his official capacity`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 466: Does it purport to be a certificate, document or electronic record made by a public servant (s 21) in his official capacity?
    `purports to be an authority to institute or defend a suit, or to take any proceedings therein, or to confess judgment`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 466: Does it purport to be an authority to institute or defend a suit, to take any proceedings in one, or to confess judgment?
    `purports to be a power of attorney`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 466: Does it purport to be a power of attorney?

    -- s 467: what the forged document purports to be
    `purports to be a valuable security`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 467: Does it purport to be a valuable security (s 30) - a cheque, a bill, a promissory note, a share transfer, a credit or ATM card?
    `purports to be a will`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 467: Does it purport to be a will (s 31)?
    `purports to be an authority to adopt a child`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 467: Does it purport to be an authority to adopt a child?
    `purports to give authority to make or transfer any valuable security, or to receive the principal, interest or dividends thereon`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 467: Does it purport to give anyone authority to make or transfer a valuable security, or to receive the principal, interest or dividends on one?
    `purports to give authority to receive or deliver any money, movable property or valuable security`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 467: Does it purport to give anyone authority to receive or deliver money, movable property (s 22) or a valuable security?
    `purports to be an acquittance or receipt acknowledging the payment of money`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 467: Does it purport to be an acquittance or a receipt acknowledging the payment of money?
    `purports to be an acquittance or receipt for the delivery of any movable property or valuable security`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 467: Does it purport to be an acquittance or a receipt for the delivery of movable property or a valuable security?

    -- s 468
    `intending that the document forged shall be used for the purpose of cheating`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 468: Did the accused intend the forged document or record to be used for the purpose of cheating (s 415 - defined in pc-property; joined at integration)? The cheating need not have happened. (Fault element.)
    -- s 469
    `intending that the document forged shall harm the reputation of any person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 469: Did the accused intend the forged document or record to harm anyone's reputation? (Fault element.)
    `knowing that it is likely to be used to harm the reputation of any person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 469: Did the accused know it was likely to be used to harm anyone's reputation? (Fault element.)

§§ `s 464 - making a false document or false electronic record`

-- 464.-(1) A person is said to make a false document or false electronic
--   record -
--   (a) who dishonestly or fraudulently -
--       (i) makes, signs, seals or executes a document or part of a document;
--       (ii) makes any electronic record or part of any electronic record;
--       (iii) affixes any electronic signature on any electronic record; or
--       (iv) makes any mark denoting the execution of a document or the
--            authenticity of the electronic signature,
--       with the intention of causing it to be believed that such document or
--       electronic record or part ... or electronic signature was made,
--       signed, sealed, executed or affixed by or by the authority of a person
--       by whom or by whose authority he knows that it was not made, signed,
--       sealed, executed or affixed, or at a time at which he knows that it
--       was not made, signed, sealed, executed or affixed;
--   (b) who without lawful authority, dishonestly or fraudulently, by
--       cancellation or otherwise, alters a document or an electronic record
--       in any material part thereof, after it has been made, executed or
--       affixed with an electronic signature, either by himself or by any
--       other person, whether that person is living or dead at the time of the
--       alteration; or
--   (c) who dishonestly or fraudulently causes any person to sign, seal,
--       execute or alter a document or an electronic record or to affix his
--       electronic signature on an electronic record, knowing that such
--       person by reason of unsoundness of mind or intoxication cannot, or
--       that by reason of deception practised upon him he does not, know the
--       contents of the document or electronic record or the nature of the
--       alteration.
--   (2) In this section, "electronic signature" has the same meaning as in
--       the Electronic Transactions Act 2010.
--   Explanation 1.-A man's signature of his own name may amount to forgery.
--   Explanation 2.-The making of a false document in the name of a fictitious
--   person, intending it to be believed that the document was made by a real
--   person, or in the name of a deceased person, intending it to be believed
--   that the document was made by the person in his lifetime, may amount to
--   forgery.
--   [Illustrations (a)-(k), Explanation 1 Illustrations (a)-(e) and the
--    Explanation 2 Illustration are the tests in pc-documents-defamation-tests.l4.]
--
-- Both Explanations widen limb (a)'s intention leaf and ride in its @desc
-- (notes/PLAN.md §3.8). s 464(2) rides in the @desc of (a)(iii).
@export Whether the accused "makes a false document or false electronic record" within section 464 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts` @desc What the accused did to the document or record, and with what intention
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `makes a false document or false electronic record` f IF
        "(1) A person is said to make a false document or false electronic record -"
   ..   (    "(a) who"
             ...  (    f's dishonestly
                  OR   f's fraudulently )
             ...  (    "(i)"   ... f's `makes, signs, seals or executes a document or part of a document`
                  OR   "(ii)"  ... f's `makes any electronic record or part of any electronic record`
                  OR   "(iii)" ... f's `affixes any electronic signature on any electronic record`
                  OR   "(iv)"  ... f's `makes any mark denoting the execution of a document or the authenticity of the electronic signature` )
             ...  "with the intention of causing it to be believed that it was made, signed, sealed, executed or affixed"
             ...  (    f's `intending it to be believed that it was made by or by the authority of a person by whom or by whose authority he knows it was not made`
                  OR   f's `intending it to be believed that it was made at a time at which he knows it was not made` ) )
   OR   (    "(b) who"
             ...  f's `without lawful authority`
             ...  (    f's dishonestly
                  OR   f's fraudulently )
             ...  f's `alters a document or an electronic record in any material part after it has been made or executed` )
   OR   (    "(c) who"
             ...  (    f's dishonestly
                  OR   f's fraudulently )
             ...  f's `causes any person to sign, seal, execute or alter a document or an electronic record, or to affix his electronic signature`
             ...  (    f's `knowing that such person by reason of unsoundness of mind or intoxication cannot know the contents or the nature of the alteration`
                  OR   f's `knowing that such person by reason of deception practised upon him does not know the contents or the nature of the alteration` ) )

§§ `s 463 - forgery`

-- 463. Whoever makes any false document or electronic record or part of a
--      document or an electronic record with intent to cause damage or injury
--      to the public or to any person, or to support any claim or title, or
--      to cause any person to part with property, or to enter into any express
--      or implied contract, or with intent to commit fraud or that fraud may
--      be committed, commits forgery.
@export Whether the accused "commits forgery" within section 463 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts` @desc What the accused made false, how, and with what intent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits forgery` f IF
        "Whoever makes any false"
   ...  (    f's `a document`
        OR   f's `an electronic record` )
   ...  "or part of a document or an electronic record"
   ...  `makes a false document or false electronic record` f
   ...  "with intent"
   ...  (    f's `with intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person`
        OR   f's `with intent to support any claim or title`
        OR   f's `with intent to cause any person to part with property`
        OR   f's `with intent to cause any person to enter into any express or implied contract`
        OR   f's `with intent to commit fraud or that fraud may be committed` )

§§ `s 465 - punishment for forgery`

-- 465. Whoever commits forgery shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
--      which may extend to 4 years, or with fine, or with both.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 465 of the Penal Code 1871 (forgery)
GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts` @desc What the accused made false, how, and with what intent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 465` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `commits forgery` f

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 465
`punishment prescribed by s 465` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, or fine, or both` "465"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 4 years, or with fine, or with both" 48

§§ `s 466 - forgery of a record of a court of justice, or a public register of births, etc.`

-- 466. Whoever forges a document or an electronic record, purporting to be a
--      record or proceeding of or before a court of justice, or a register of
--      birth, baptism, marriage or burial, or a register kept by a public
--      servant as such, or a certificate or document or an electronic record,
--      purporting to be made by a public servant in his official capacity, or
--      an authority to institute or defend a suit, or to take any proceedings
--      therein, or to confess judgment, or a power of attorney, shall be
--      punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and
--      shall also be liable to fine.
@export Whether a forged document or electronic record is of a description mentioned in section 466 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts` @desc What the forged thing purports to be
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the document is of a description mentioned in section 466` f IF
        "purporting to be"
   ..   f's `purports to be a record or proceeding of or before a court of justice`
   OR   f's `purports to be a register of birth, baptism, marriage or burial`
   OR   f's `purports to be a register kept by a public servant as such`
   OR   f's `purports to be a certificate or document made by a public servant in his official capacity`
   OR   f's `purports to be an authority to institute or defend a suit, or to take any proceedings therein, or to confess judgment`
   OR   f's `purports to be a power of attorney`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 466 of the Penal Code 1871 (forgery of a record of a court of justice, or a public register of births, etc.)
GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts` @desc What the accused made false, how, with what intent, and what it purports to be
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 466` f IF
        "Whoever forges a document or an electronic record,"
   ...  `commits forgery` f
   ...  `the document is of a description mentioned in section 466` f

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 466
`punishment prescribed by s 466` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "466"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine" 120

§§ `s 467 - forgery of a valuable security or will`

-- 467. Whoever forges a document which purports to be a valuable security or
--      a will, or an authority to adopt a child, or which purports to give
--      authority to any person to make or transfer any valuable security, or
--      to receive the principal, interest, or dividends thereon, or to receive
--      or deliver any money, movable property, or valuable security, or any
--      document purporting to be an acquittance or a receipt, acknowledging
--      the payment of money, or an acquittance or a receipt for the delivery
--      of any movable property or valuable security, shall be punished with
--      imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall also be
--      liable to fine.
--
-- "forges a document" - not "or an electronic record", as ss 466, 468, 469
-- say. So the thing forged must be a document (FORK DD-4).
@export Whether a forged document is of a description mentioned in section 467 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts` @desc What the forged document purports to be
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the document is of a description mentioned in section 467` f IF
        "a document which purports to be"
   ..   f's `purports to be a valuable security`
   OR   f's `purports to be a will`
   OR   f's `purports to be an authority to adopt a child`
   OR   "or which purports to give authority to any person"
        ... (    f's `purports to give authority to make or transfer any valuable security, or to receive the principal, interest or dividends thereon`
             OR  f's `purports to give authority to receive or deliver any money, movable property or valuable security` )
   OR   "or any document purporting to be"
        ... (    f's `purports to be an acquittance or receipt acknowledging the payment of money`
             OR  f's `purports to be an acquittance or receipt for the delivery of any movable property or valuable security` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 467 of the Penal Code 1871 (forgery of a valuable security or will)
GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts` @desc What the accused made false, how, with what intent, and what it purports to be
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 467` f IF
        "Whoever forges a"
   ...  f's `a document`
   ...  `commits forgery` f
   ...  `the document is of a description mentioned in section 467` f

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 467
`punishment prescribed by s 467` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "467"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall also be liable to fine" 180

§§ `s 468 - forgery for the purpose of cheating`

-- 468. Whoever commits forgery, intending that the document or electronic
--      record forged shall be used for the purpose of cheating, shall be
--      punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and
--      shall also be liable to fine.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 468 of the Penal Code 1871 (forgery for the purpose of cheating)
GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts` @desc What the accused made false, how, and with what intent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 468` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `commits forgery` f
   ...  f's `intending that the document forged shall be used for the purpose of cheating`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 468
`punishment prescribed by s 468` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "468"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine" 120

§§ `s 469 - forgery for the purpose of harming the reputation of any person`

-- 469. Whoever commits forgery, intending that the document or electronic
--      record forged shall harm the reputation of any person, or knowing that
--      it is likely to be used for that purpose, shall be punished with
--      imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, and shall also be
--      liable to fine.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 469 of the Penal Code 1871 (forgery for the purpose of harming the reputation of any person)
GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts` @desc What the accused made false, how, and with what intent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 469` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `commits forgery` f
   ...  (    f's `intending that the document forged shall harm the reputation of any person`
        OR   f's `knowing that it is likely to be used to harm the reputation of any person` )

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 469
`punishment prescribed by s 469` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "469"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, and shall also be liable to fine" 60

§§ `s 470 - "a forged document" or "a forged electronic record"`

-- 470. A false document or false electronic record, made wholly or in part by
--      forgery, is designated "a forged document" or "a forged electronic
--      record", respectively.
--
-- A definition only: no charge. Read by s 471 and s 474, whose facts record
-- carries "knows it to be a forged document" as a leaf.
@export Whether a thing the accused made is "a forged document" or "a forged electronic record" within section 470 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts` @desc How the thing was made false, and with what intent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a forged document or forged electronic record within section 470` f IF
        "A false document or false electronic record,"
   ...  `makes a false document or false electronic record` f
   ...  "made wholly or in part by"
   ...  `commits forgery` f

§§ `The facts of using or holding a forged document - ss 471, 474`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 471, 474 - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC ss 124-125 require
DECLARE `Forged Document Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the document`        IS A STRING  @desc The forged document or electronic record, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "a Certificate of Entitlement purporting to be issued by the Land Transport Authority"
    `the use`             IS A STRING  @desc How the accused used it, as it is to read after "by" - for example "submitting it to Lim Motor Pte Ltd"; leave blank for a charge of possession
    `a document`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a document (s 29)?
    `an electronic record`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing an electronic record (s 29B)?
    `knows it to be a forged document or forged electronic record`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know it to be forged - a false document or record made wholly or partly by forgery (ss 463, 470)? (Fault element.)
    `has reason to believe it to be a forged document or forged electronic record`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused have reason to believe (s 26) it to be forged? (Fault element; s 471 only - s 474 requires knowledge.)
    -- s 471
    `uses as genuine`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 471: Did the accused use it as genuine? (Physical element.)
    dishonestly           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act dishonestly (s 24)? (Fault element.)
    fraudulently          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act fraudulently (s 25)? (Fault element.)
    -- s 474
    `has in his possession`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 474: Did the accused have it in his possession (s 27: including through a spouse, clerk or servant)? (Physical element.)
    `intending that the same shall fraudulently or dishonestly be used as genuine`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 474: Did the accused intend it to be used, fraudulently or dishonestly, as genuine? (Fault element.)
    -- the descriptions in s 466 and s 467, which choose the punishment (s 471) or make the offence (s 474)
    `purports to be a record or proceeding of or before a court of justice`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 466: Does it purport to be a record or proceeding of or before a court of justice?
    `purports to be a register of birth, baptism, marriage or burial`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 466: Does it purport to be a register of birth, baptism, marriage or burial?
    `purports to be a register kept by a public servant as such`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 466: Does it purport to be a register kept by a public servant as such?
    `purports to be a certificate or document made by a public servant in his official capacity`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 466: Does it purport to be a certificate, document or electronic record made by a public servant in his official capacity?
    `purports to be an authority to institute or defend a suit, or to take any proceedings therein, or to confess judgment`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 466: Does it purport to be an authority to institute or defend a suit, to take proceedings in one, or to confess judgment?
    `purports to be a power of attorney`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 466: Does it purport to be a power of attorney?
    `purports to be a valuable security`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 467: Does it purport to be a valuable security (s 30)?
    `purports to be a will`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 467: Does it purport to be a will (s 31)?
    `purports to be an authority to adopt a child`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 467: Does it purport to be an authority to adopt a child?
    `purports to give authority to make or transfer any valuable security, or to receive the principal, interest or dividends thereon`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 467: Does it purport to give authority to make or transfer a valuable security, or to receive the principal, interest or dividends on one?
    `purports to give authority to receive or deliver any money, movable property or valuable security`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 467: Does it purport to give authority to receive or deliver money, movable property or a valuable security?
    `purports to be an acquittance or receipt acknowledging the payment of money`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 467: Does it purport to be an acquittance or receipt acknowledging the payment of money?
    `purports to be an acquittance or receipt for the delivery of any movable property or valuable security`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 467: Does it purport to be an acquittance or receipt for the delivery of movable property or a valuable security?

@export Whether a forged document or electronic record held or used is of a description mentioned in section 466 of the Penal Code 1871 (as ss 471 and 474 read it)
GIVEN f IS A `Forged Document Facts` @desc What the forged thing purports to be
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the forged document is of a description mentioned in section 466` f IF
        "one of the descriptions mentioned in section 466"
   ..   f's `purports to be a record or proceeding of or before a court of justice`
   OR   f's `purports to be a register of birth, baptism, marriage or burial`
   OR   f's `purports to be a register kept by a public servant as such`
   OR   f's `purports to be a certificate or document made by a public servant in his official capacity`
   OR   f's `purports to be an authority to institute or defend a suit, or to take any proceedings therein, or to confess judgment`
   OR   f's `purports to be a power of attorney`

@export Whether a forged document held or used is of a description mentioned in section 467 of the Penal Code 1871 (as ss 471 and 474 read it)
GIVEN f IS A `Forged Document Facts` @desc What the forged document purports to be
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the forged document is of a description mentioned in section 467` f IF
        "the document is one of the descriptions mentioned in section 467"
   ...  f's `a document`
   ...  (    f's `purports to be a valuable security`
        OR   f's `purports to be a will`
        OR   f's `purports to be an authority to adopt a child`
        OR   f's `purports to give authority to make or transfer any valuable security, or to receive the principal, interest or dividends thereon`
        OR   f's `purports to give authority to receive or deliver any money, movable property or valuable security`
        OR   f's `purports to be an acquittance or receipt acknowledging the payment of money`
        OR   f's `purports to be an acquittance or receipt for the delivery of any movable property or valuable security` )

§§ `s 471 - using as genuine a forged document or forged electronic record`

-- 471. Whoever fraudulently or dishonestly uses as genuine any document or
--      electronic record which he knows or has reason to believe to be a
--      forged document or forged electronic record, shall be punished in the
--      same manner as if he had forged such document or electronic record.
--
-- "in the same manner as if he had forged such document": the punishment of
-- s 467, s 466 or s 465, chosen by what the document purports to be (FORK
-- DD-3 - not s 468 or s 469, which turn on the forger's intent).
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 471 of the Penal Code 1871 (using as genuine a forged document or forged electronic record)
GIVEN f IS A `Forged Document Facts` @desc The forged document, what the accused knew of it, and how he used it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 471` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  (    f's fraudulently
        OR   f's dishonestly )
   ...  f's `uses as genuine`
   ...  "any"
   ...  (    f's `a document`
        OR   f's `an electronic record` )
   ...  "which he"
   ...  (    f's `knows it to be a forged document or forged electronic record`
        OR   f's `has reason to believe it to be a forged document or forged electronic record` )

GIVEN f IS A `Forged Document Facts`
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment under s 471` f MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the forged document is of a description mentioned in section 467` f
        THEN `punishment prescribed by s 467`
        IF   `the forged document is of a description mentioned in section 466` f
        THEN `punishment prescribed by s 466`
        OTHERWISE `punishment prescribed by s 465`

§§ `ss 472, 473 - making or possessing a counterfeit seal, plate, etc.`

-- 472. Whoever makes or counterfeits any seal, plate or other instrument for
--      making an impression, intending that the same shall be used for the
--      purpose of committing any forgery which would be punishable under
--      section 467, or with such intent has in his possession any such seal,
--      plate or other instrument, knowing the same to be counterfeit, shall be
--      punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years,
--      and shall also be liable to fine.
-- 473. [The same] ... any forgery which would be punishable under any section
--      of this Chapter other than section 467 ... 10 years, and shall also be
--      liable to fine.
@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 472, 473 - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC ss 124-125 require
DECLARE `Counterfeit Seal Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the instrument`      IS A STRING  @desc The seal, plate or other instrument, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "a rubber stamp bearing the seal of the Registry of Marriages"
    `makes or counterfeits any seal, plate or other instrument for making an impression`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make, or counterfeit (s 28), a seal, plate or other instrument for making an impression? (Physical element.)
    `has in his possession any such seal, plate or other instrument`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused have such a seal, plate or instrument in his possession (s 27)? (Physical element.)
    `knowing the same to be counterfeit`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know it to be counterfeit (s 28)? Required for the possession limb only. (Fault element.)
    `intending that it shall be used for committing a forgery punishable under section 467`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend it to be used to commit a forgery that would be punishable under s 467 (a valuable security, a will, and the like)? (Fault element.)
    `intending that it shall be used for committing a forgery punishable under another section of this Chapter`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend it to be used to commit a forgery that would be punishable under a section of Chapter 18 other than s 467? (Fault element.)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 472 of the Penal Code 1871 (making or possessing a counterfeit seal, plate, etc., with intent to commit a forgery punishable under section 467)
GIVEN f IS A `Counterfeit Seal Facts` @desc The instrument, what the accused did with it, and what he intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 472` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  (    f's `makes or counterfeits any seal, plate or other instrument for making an impression`
        OR   "or with such intent"
             ...  f's `has in his possession any such seal, plate or other instrument`
             ...  f's `knowing the same to be counterfeit` )
   ...  f's `intending that it shall be used for committing a forgery punishable under section 467`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 472
`punishment prescribed by s 472` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "472"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall also be liable to fine" 180

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 473 of the Penal Code 1871 (making or possessing a counterfeit seal, plate, etc., with intent to commit a forgery punishable otherwise)
GIVEN f IS A `Counterfeit Seal Facts` @desc The instrument, what the accused did with it, and what he intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 473` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  (    f's `makes or counterfeits any seal, plate or other instrument for making an impression`
        OR   "or with such intent"
             ...  f's `has in his possession any such seal, plate or other instrument`
             ...  f's `knowing the same to be counterfeit` )
   ...  f's `intending that it shall be used for committing a forgery punishable under another section of this Chapter`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 473
`punishment prescribed by s 473` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "473"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine" 120

§§ `ss 473A-473C - equipment for making a false instrument`

-- 473A. Whoever makes or has in his custody or under his control a machine or
--       implement, or paper or other material, which to his knowledge is or
--       has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of any false
--       instrument shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
--       extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- 473B. Any person (A) who -
--       (a) makes or has in his custody or under his control a machine or
--           implement, or paper or other material, which is or has been
--           specifically designed or adapted for the making of any
--           instrument; and
--       (b) intends that -
--           (i) he or another person makes a false instrument using the
--               machine or implement, or paper or other material in order to
--               induce another person (B) to accept it as genuine; and
--           (ii) by reason of so accepting it, B does or does not do some act
--               to B's or any other person's prejudice,
--       shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to
--       10 years, or with fine, or with both.
--
-- "false instrument" is not defined; "instrument" is (s 31A, for Chapters 12
-- and 18). FORK DD-5.
@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 473A, 473B - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC ss 124-125 require
DECLARE `False Instrument Equipment Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the equipment`       IS A STRING  @desc The machine, implement, paper or material, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "a card embosser and 40 blank magnetic-stripe cards"
    `makes it`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make the machine, implement, paper or material? (Physical element.)
    `has it in his custody or under his control`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused have it in his custody or under his control? (Physical element.)
    -- s 473A
    `to his knowledge it is or has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of any false instrument`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 473A: Did the accused know that it is, or has been, specifically designed or adapted for making a false instrument (an instrument, s 31A, made false as s 464 describes)? (Fault element.)
    -- s 473B
    `it is or has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of any instrument`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 473B(a): Is it, or has it been, specifically designed or adapted for making an instrument (s 31A)? No knowledge of this is required by (a). (Physical element.)
    `intends that he or another person makes a false instrument using it in order to induce another person to accept it as genuine`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 473B(b)(i): Did the accused intend that he or someone else would use it to make a false instrument, to induce another person (B) - or a machine (s 473C(3)) - to accept it as genuine? (Fault element.)
    `intends that by reason of so accepting it, that person does or does not do some act to his or any other person's prejudice`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 473B(b)(ii): Did the accused intend that, by accepting it as genuine, B would do or not do some act to B's or anyone else's prejudice (s 473C - drill down with `to a person's prejudice within section 473C`)? (Fault element.)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 473A of the Penal Code 1871 (making or possessing equipment for making a false instrument)
GIVEN f IS A `False Instrument Equipment Facts` @desc The equipment, what the accused did with it, and what he knew of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 473A` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  (    f's `makes it`
        OR   f's `has it in his custody or under his control` )
   ...  "a machine or implement, or paper or other material, which"
   ...  f's `to his knowledge it is or has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of any false instrument`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 473A
`punishment prescribed by s 473A` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, or fine, or both` "473A"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with both" 60

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 473B of the Penal Code 1871 (making or possessing equipment for making a false instrument with intent to induce prejudice)
GIVEN f IS A `False Instrument Equipment Facts` @desc The equipment, what the accused did with it, and what he intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 473B` f IF
        "Any person (A) who -"
   ...  (    "(a)"
             ...  (    f's `makes it`
                  OR   f's `has it in his custody or under his control` )
             ...  f's `it is or has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of any instrument` )
   ...  (    "and (b) intends that -"
             ...  "(i)" ... f's `intends that he or another person makes a false instrument using it in order to induce another person to accept it as genuine`
             ...  "and (ii)" ... f's `intends that by reason of so accepting it, that person does or does not do some act to his or any other person's prejudice` )

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 473B
`punishment prescribed by s 473B` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, or fine, or both` "473B"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, or with fine, or with both" 120

-- 473C.-(1) For the purposes of section 473B and subject to subsections (2)
--   and (4), an act or omission intended to be induced is to a person's
--   prejudice if, and only if, it is one which, if it occurs, will -
--   (a) result in his permanent or temporary loss of property;
--   (b) result in his being deprived of an opportunity to earn remuneration or
--       greater remuneration;
--   (c) result in his being deprived of an opportunity to gain a financial
--       advantage otherwise than by way of remuneration;
--   (d) result in somebody being given an opportunity to earn remuneration or
--       greater remuneration from him;
--   (e) result in somebody being given an opportunity to gain a financial
--       advantage from him otherwise than by way of remuneration; or
--   (f) be the result of his having accepted a false instrument as genuine in
--       connection with his performance of any duty.
--   (2) ... an act which a person has an enforceable duty to do and an
--       omission to do an act which a person is not entitled to do shall be
--       disregarded.
--   (3) The reference in section 473B to inducing a person (B) to accept a
--       false instrument as genuine includes a reference to inducing a
--       machine to respond to an instrument as if it were a genuine
--       instrument.
--   (4) Where subsection (3) applies, the act or omission intended to be
--       induced by the machine responding to the instrument shall be treated
--       as an act or omission to a person's prejudice.
--   (5) In subsection (1)(a), "loss" includes a loss by not getting what one
--       might get, as well as a loss by parting with what one has.
--
-- A definition, for s 473B's drill-down; no charge. (3) widens s 473B(b)(i)'s
-- leaf and rides in its @desc; (5) rides in the @desc of (a).
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 473C - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Prejudice Facts` HAS
    `result in his permanent or temporary loss of property`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (1)(a) Would the act or omission result in the person's permanent or temporary loss of property - including not getting what he might get, as well as parting with what he has (s 473C(5))?
    `result in his being deprived of an opportunity to earn remuneration or greater remuneration`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (1)(b) Would it deprive him of an opportunity to earn remuneration or greater remuneration?
    `result in his being deprived of an opportunity to gain a financial advantage otherwise than by way of remuneration`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (1)(c) Would it deprive him of an opportunity to gain a financial advantage otherwise than by remuneration?
    `result in somebody being given an opportunity to earn remuneration or greater remuneration from him`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (1)(d) Would it give somebody an opportunity to earn remuneration or greater remuneration from him?
    `result in somebody being given an opportunity to gain a financial advantage from him otherwise than by way of remuneration`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (1)(e) Would it give somebody an opportunity to gain a financial advantage from him otherwise than by remuneration?
    `be the result of his having accepted a false instrument as genuine in connection with his performance of any duty`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (1)(f) Would it be the result of his having accepted a false instrument as genuine in connection with performing a duty?
    `an act which the person has an enforceable duty to do`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (2) Is it an act the person has an enforceable duty to do? If so it is disregarded.
    `an omission to do an act which the person is not entitled to do`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (2) Is it an omission to do an act the person is not entitled to do? If so it is disregarded.
    `induced by a machine responding to the instrument`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (3), (4) Is the act or omission one intended to be induced by a machine responding to the instrument as if it were genuine? If so it is treated as to a person's prejudice.

@export Whether an act or omission intended to be induced is "to a person's prejudice" within section 473C of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN p IS A `Prejudice Facts` @desc What the act or omission would result in, if it occurred
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `to a person's prejudice within section 473C` p IF
        (    "(4) Where subsection (3) applies, ... shall be treated as an act or omission to a person's prejudice."
        ...  p's `induced by a machine responding to the instrument` )
   OR   (    "(1) ... is to a person's prejudice if, and only if, it is one which, if it occurs, will -"
        ...  (    "(a)" ... p's `result in his permanent or temporary loss of property`
             OR   "(b)" ... p's `result in his being deprived of an opportunity to earn remuneration or greater remuneration`
             OR   "(c)" ... p's `result in his being deprived of an opportunity to gain a financial advantage otherwise than by way of remuneration`
             OR   "(d)" ... p's `result in somebody being given an opportunity to earn remuneration or greater remuneration from him`
             OR   "(e)" ... p's `result in somebody being given an opportunity to gain a financial advantage from him otherwise than by way of remuneration`
             OR   "(f)" ... p's `be the result of his having accepted a false instrument as genuine in connection with his performance of any duty` )
        ...  "(2) ... shall be disregarded"
        ...  NOT p's `an act which the person has an enforceable duty to do`
        ...  NOT p's `an omission to do an act which the person is not entitled to do` )

§§ `s 474 - having possession of a forged document, with intent to use it as genuine`

-- 474. Whoever has in his possession any document or electronic record,
--      knowing the same to be forged, and intending that the same shall
--      fraudulently or dishonestly be used as genuine, shall, if the document
--      or electronic record is one of the descriptions mentioned in section
--      466, be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to
--      10 years, and shall also be liable to fine; and if the document is one
--      of the descriptions mentioned in section 467, shall be punished with
--      imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall also be
--      liable to fine.
--
-- The description is an ELEMENT here (no description, no offence) and also
-- chooses the punishment. A document of both descriptions takes s 467's
-- (FORK DD-6).
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 474 of the Penal Code 1871 (having possession of a forged document or electronic record of a description in section 466 or 467, with intent to use it as genuine)
GIVEN f IS A `Forged Document Facts` @desc The forged document, what the accused knew of it, and what he intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 474` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  f's `has in his possession`
   ...  "any"
   ...  (    f's `a document`
        OR   f's `an electronic record` )
   ...  f's `knows it to be a forged document or forged electronic record`
   ...  f's `intending that the same shall fraudulently or dishonestly be used as genuine`
   ...  "shall, if the document or electronic record is"
   ...  (    `the forged document is of a description mentioned in section 466` f
        OR   `the forged document is of a description mentioned in section 467` f )

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 474, first limb - a document or electronic record of a description in s 466
`punishment prescribed by s 474, for a document of a description in section 466` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "474"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine" 120

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 474, second limb - a document of a description in s 467
`punishment prescribed by s 474, for a document of a description in section 467` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "474"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall also be liable to fine" 180

GIVEN f IS A `Forged Document Facts`
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment under s 474` f MEANS
    IF   `the forged document is of a description mentioned in section 467` f
    THEN `punishment prescribed by s 474, for a document of a description in section 467`
    ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 474, for a document of a description in section 466`

§§ `ss 475, 476 - counterfeiting an authenticating device or mark`

-- 475. Whoever counterfeits upon or in the substance of any material any
--      device or mark used for the purpose of authenticating any document
--      described in section 467, intending that such device or mark shall be
--      used for the purpose of giving the appearance of authenticity to any
--      document then forged or thereafter to be forged on such material, or
--      who with such intent has in his possession any material upon or in the
--      substance of which any such device or mark has been counterfeited,
--      shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to
--      15 years, and shall also be liable to fine.
-- 476. [The same, for] any document or electronic record other than the
--      documents described in section 467 ... 10 years, and shall also be
--      liable to fine.
@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 475, 476 - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC ss 124-125 require
DECLARE `Counterfeit Mark Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the material`        IS A STRING  @desc The material and the device or mark, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "200 sheets of paper bearing a counterfeit watermark of the Monetary Authority of Singapore"
    `counterfeits upon or in the substance of any material any device or mark used for the purpose of authenticating a document`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused counterfeit (s 28), on or in the substance of any material, a device or mark used to authenticate a document? (Physical element.)
    `has in his possession any material upon or in the substance of which any such device or mark has been counterfeited`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused have in his possession (s 27) material on or in which such a device or mark had been counterfeited? (Physical element.)
    `intending that the device or mark shall be used to give the appearance of authenticity to a document then forged or thereafter to be forged on the material`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend the device or mark to be used to give the appearance of authenticity to a document forged, or to be forged, on that material? (Fault element.)
    `the device or mark is used for authenticating a document described in section 467`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 475: Is the device or mark one used to authenticate a document described in s 467 (a valuable security, a will, and the like)?
    `the device or mark is used for authenticating a document or electronic record other than those described in section 467`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 476: Is the device or mark one used to authenticate a document or electronic record OTHER than those described in s 467?

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 475 of the Penal Code 1871 (counterfeiting a device or mark used for authenticating documents described in section 467, or possessing counterfeit marked material)
GIVEN f IS A `Counterfeit Mark Facts` @desc The material, the device or mark, and what the accused intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 475` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  (    f's `counterfeits upon or in the substance of any material any device or mark used for the purpose of authenticating a document`
        OR   "or who with such intent"
             ...  f's `has in his possession any material upon or in the substance of which any such device or mark has been counterfeited` )
   ...  f's `the device or mark is used for authenticating a document described in section 467`
   ...  f's `intending that the device or mark shall be used to give the appearance of authenticity to a document then forged or thereafter to be forged on the material`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 475
`punishment prescribed by s 475` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "475"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall also be liable to fine" 180

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 476 of the Penal Code 1871 (counterfeiting a device or mark used for authenticating documents or electronic records other than those described in section 467, or possessing counterfeit marked material)
GIVEN f IS A `Counterfeit Mark Facts` @desc The material, the device or mark, and what the accused intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 476` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  (    f's `counterfeits upon or in the substance of any material any device or mark used for the purpose of authenticating a document`
        OR   "or who with such intent"
             ...  f's `has in his possession any material upon or in the substance of which any such device or mark has been counterfeited` )
   ...  f's `the device or mark is used for authenticating a document or electronic record other than those described in section 467`
   ...  f's `intending that the device or mark shall be used to give the appearance of authenticity to a document then forged or thereafter to be forged on the material`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 476
`punishment prescribed by s 476` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "476"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine" 120

§§ `s 477 - fraudulent cancellation, destruction, etc., of a will`

-- 477. Whoever fraudulently or dishonestly, or with intent to cause damage or
--      injury to the public or to any person, cancels, destroys, or defaces,
--      or attempts to cancel, destroy, or deface, or secretes, or attempts to
--      secrete any document which is or purports to be a will, or an
--      authority to adopt a child, or any valuable security, or commits
--      mischief in respect to such document, shall be punished with
--      imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall also be
--      liable to fine.
--
-- The attempts are the section's own words, so they are leaves here, not
-- s 511 riders.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 477 - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC ss 124-125 require
DECLARE `Will or Security Destruction Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the document`        IS A STRING  @desc The document, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "the last will of Tan Ah Kow dated 1 May 2015"
    `the act`             IS A STRING  @desc What the accused did to it, as it is to read after "did" - for example "destroy"
    fraudulently          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act fraudulently (s 25)? (Fault element.)
    dishonestly           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act dishonestly (s 24)? (Fault element.)
    `with intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act intending to cause damage or injury (s 44) to the public or to any person? (Fault element.)
    `cancels, destroys or defaces`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cancel, destroy or deface the document?
    `attempts to cancel, destroy or deface`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused attempt to cancel, destroy or deface it?
    secretes              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused secrete (hide) it?
    `attempts to secrete` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused attempt to secrete it?
    `commits mischief in respect to such document`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused commit mischief (s 425 - defined in pc-property; joined at integration) in respect of it?
    `is or purports to be a will`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it, or does it purport to be, a will (s 31)?
    `is or purports to be an authority to adopt a child`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it, or does it purport to be, an authority to adopt a child?
    `is or purports to be a valuable security`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it, or does it purport to be, a valuable security (s 30)? (FORK DD-7)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 477 of the Penal Code 1871 (fraudulent cancellation, destruction, etc., of a will)
GIVEN f IS A `Will or Security Destruction Facts` @desc The document, what the accused did to it, and with what intent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 477` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  (    f's fraudulently
        OR   f's dishonestly
        OR   f's `with intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person` )
   ...  (    f's `cancels, destroys or defaces`
        OR   f's `attempts to cancel, destroy or deface`
        OR   f's secretes
        OR   f's `attempts to secrete`
        OR   "or commits mischief in respect to such document"
             ...  f's `commits mischief in respect to such document` )
   ...  "any document which is or purports to be"
   ...  (    f's `is or purports to be a will`
        OR   f's `is or purports to be an authority to adopt a child`
        OR   f's `is or purports to be a valuable security` )

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 477
`punishment prescribed by s 477` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, and liability to fine` "477"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall also be liable to fine" 180

§§ `s 477A - falsification of accounts`

-- 477A. Whoever, being a clerk, officer or servant, or employed or acting in
--   the capacity of a clerk, officer or servant, intentionally and with intent
--   to defraud destroys, alters, conceals, mutilates or falsifies any book,
--   electronic record, paper, writing, valuable security or account or a set
--   thereof which belongs to or is in the possession of his employer, or has
--   been received by him for or on behalf of his employer, or intentionally
--   and with intent to defraud makes or abets the making of any false entry
--   in, or omits or alters or abets the omission or alteration of any material
--   particular from or in any such book, electronic record, paper, writing,
--   valuable security or account or a set thereof, shall be punished with
--   imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, or with fine, or
--   with both.
--   Explanation 1.-It shall be sufficient in any charge under this section to
--   allege a general intent to defraud without naming any particular person
--   intended to be defrauded, or specifying any particular sum of money
--   intended to be the subject of the fraud or any particular day on which
--   the offence was committed.
--   Explanation 2.-Any books, electronic records, papers, writings, valuable
--   securities or accounts or any combination thereof form a set if they serve
--   the same function or purpose in relation to the employer's affairs or
--   business.
--
-- Explanation 1 is a rule of pleading: the charge builder names no person
-- defrauded and no sum. Explanation 2 widens the object leaf.
-- "any such book ..." in the second limb carries the employer condition over
-- (FORK DD-8).
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 477A - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC ss 124-125 require
DECLARE `Falsification of Accounts Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the capacity`        IS A STRING  @desc The accused's position, as it is to read after "being" - for example "a servant, to wit, an accounts executive of Tan Holdings Pte Ltd"
    `the falsification`   IS A STRING  @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "did intentionally and with intent to defraud" - for example "make a false entry in a payment voucher dated 3 March 2020, to wit, by recording a payment of $5,000 to Lim Trading, when no such payment was due"
    `being a clerk, officer or servant`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused a clerk, officer or servant?
    `employed or acting in the capacity of a clerk, officer or servant`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused employed, or acting, in the capacity of a clerk, officer or servant?
    `acts intentionally`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused do the act intentionally (s 26C)? (Fault element.)
    `with intent to defraud`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act with intent to defraud? A general intent suffices; no particular person or sum need be identified (Explanation 1). (Fault element; FORK DD-9.)
    -- the first limb
    `destroys, alters, conceals, mutilates or falsifies`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused destroy, alter, conceal, mutilate or falsify the book, record, paper, writing, security or account? (Physical element.)
    -- the second limb
    `makes or abets the making of any false entry in`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make, or abet (s 107 - defined in pc-general-part; joined at integration) the making of, a false entry in it? (Physical element.)
    `omits or alters or abets the omission or alteration of any material particular from or in`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused omit or alter, or abet the omission or alteration of, a material particular from or in it? (Physical element.)
    -- the object
    `any book, electronic record, paper, writing, valuable security or account or a set thereof`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a book, electronic record (s 29B), paper, writing, valuable security (s 30) or account - or a set of them, serving the same function or purpose in the employer's affairs or business (Explanation 2)?
    `belongs to or is in the possession of his employer`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it belong to, or is it in the possession of, the accused's employer?
    `has been received by him for or on behalf of his employer`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it received by the accused for or on behalf of his employer?

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 477A of the Penal Code 1871 (falsification of accounts)
GIVEN f IS A `Falsification of Accounts Facts` @desc The accused's position, what he did to his employer's records, and with what intent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 477A` f IF
        "Whoever, being"
   ...  (    f's `being a clerk, officer or servant`
        OR   f's `employed or acting in the capacity of a clerk, officer or servant` )
   ...  f's `acts intentionally`
   ...  "and"
   ...  f's `with intent to defraud`
   ...  (    f's `destroys, alters, conceals, mutilates or falsifies`
        OR   "or ... makes or abets the making of any false entry in, or omits or alters ..."
             ...  (    f's `makes or abets the making of any false entry in`
                  OR   f's `omits or alters or abets the omission or alteration of any material particular from or in` ) )
   ...  f's `any book, electronic record, paper, writing, valuable security or account or a set thereof`
   ...  "which"
   ...  (    f's `belongs to or is in the possession of his employer`
        OR   f's `has been received by him for or on behalf of his employer` )

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 477A
`punishment prescribed by s 477A` MEANS
    `a punishment of imprisonment, or fine, or both` "477A"
        "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, or with fine, or with both" 120

§ `The charges - forgery (ss 465-477A)`

§§ `Forgery - ss 465-469`

-- CPC s 125: forgery is an offence of deception, so the manner is recited.
-- "did commit forgery by making a false document, to wit, <the document>,
--  <the manner>, with intent to <the s 463 intents>"
GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the manner of the forgery` f MEANS
    CONCAT "did commit forgery by making a false ", (`the kind of thing forged` f), ", to wit, ", f's `the document`,
           (`the manner clause` f),
           ", with intent ", (`the intents of the forgery` f)

GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the kind of thing forged` f MEANS
    IF   f's `a document`
    THEN "document"
    ELSE "electronic record"

GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the manner clause` f MEANS
    IF   f's `the manner` EQUALS ""
    THEN ""
    ELSE CONCAT ", ", f's `the manner`

GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the intents of the forgery` f MEANS
    `joined with` ", and " (concat (LIST
        (`included if` (f's `with intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person`) "to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person"),
        (`included if` (f's `with intent to support any claim or title`) "to support a claim or title"),
        (`included if` (f's `with intent to cause any person to part with property`) "to cause any person to part with property"),
        (`included if` (f's `with intent to cause any person to enter into any express or implied contract`) "to cause any person to enter into an express or implied contract"),
        (`included if` (f's `with intent to commit fraud or that fraud may be committed`) "to commit fraud or that fraud may be committed")))

GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of forgery not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `a document` OR f's `an electronic record`) "a document or an electronic record"),
        (`missing unless` (`makes a false document or false electronic record` f) "makes a false document or false electronic record (section 464)"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `with intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person` OR f's `with intent to support any claim or title` OR f's `with intent to cause any person to part with property` OR f's `with intent to cause any person to enter into any express or implied contract` OR f's `with intent to commit fraud or that fraud may be committed`)
            "with intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person, or to support any claim or title, or to cause any person to part with property, or to enter into any express or implied contract, or with intent to commit fraud or that fraud may be committed"),
        (`missing unless` (`commits forgery` f) "the elements of section 463 taken together"))

@export Frame a charge under section 465 of the Penal Code 1871 (forgery), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts` @desc The false document, how and why it was made, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 465` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "465" "forgery"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 465`'s words)
        (`offence under s 465` f)
        (`the manner of the forgery` f)
        (`elements of forgery not made out` f)

@export Frame a charge under section 466 of the Penal Code 1871 (forgery of a record of a court of justice, or a public register of births, etc.), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts` @desc The false document, what it purports to be, how and why it was made, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 466` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "466" "forgery of a record of a court of justice, or a public register of births, etc."
        (`punishment prescribed by s 466`'s words)
        (`offence under s 466` f)
        (`the manner of the forgery` f)
        (concat (LIST (`elements of forgery not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (`the document is of a description mentioned in section 466` f) "purporting to be a record or proceeding of a court of justice, a register of birth, baptism, marriage or burial, a register kept by a public servant, a certificate or document made by a public servant in his official capacity, an authority to institute or defend a suit or to confess judgment, or a power of attorney")))

@export Frame a charge under section 467 of the Penal Code 1871 (forgery of a valuable security or will), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts` @desc The false document, what it purports to be, how and why it was made, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 467` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "467" "forgery of a valuable security or will"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 467`'s words)
        (`offence under s 467` f)
        (`the manner of the forgery` f)
        (concat (LIST (`elements of forgery not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `a document`) "a document (section 467 does not extend to an electronic record)"),
                      (`missing unless` (`the document is of a description mentioned in section 467` f) "which purports to be a valuable security, a will, an authority to adopt a child, an authority to make or transfer a valuable security or to receive or deliver money, movable property or a valuable security, or an acquittance or receipt")))

@export Frame a charge under section 468 of the Penal Code 1871 (forgery for the purpose of cheating), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts` @desc The false document, how and why it was made, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 468` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "468" "forgery for the purpose of cheating"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 468`'s words)
        (`offence under s 468` f)
        (CONCAT (`the manner of the forgery` f), ", intending that the said ", (`the kind of thing forged` f), " shall be used for the purpose of cheating")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of forgery not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `intending that the document forged shall be used for the purpose of cheating`) "intending that the document or electronic record forged shall be used for the purpose of cheating")))

@export Frame a charge under section 469 of the Penal Code 1871 (forgery for the purpose of harming the reputation of any person), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Forgery Facts` @desc The false document, how and why it was made, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 469` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "469" "forgery for the purpose of harming the reputation of any person"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 469`'s words)
        (`offence under s 469` f)
        (CONCAT (`the manner of the forgery` f), ", ",
                (IF   f's `intending that the document forged shall harm the reputation of any person`
                 THEN "intending that the said forged document shall harm the reputation of any person"
                 ELSE "knowing that the said forged document is likely to be used to harm the reputation of any person"))
        (concat (LIST (`elements of forgery not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `intending that the document forged shall harm the reputation of any person` OR f's `knowing that it is likely to be used to harm the reputation of any person`) "intending that the document or electronic record forged shall harm the reputation of any person, or knowing that it is likely to be used for that purpose")))

§§ `Using or holding a forged document - ss 471, 474`

GIVEN f IS A `Forged Document Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the kind of forged thing` f MEANS
    IF   f's `a document`
    THEN "document"
    ELSE "electronic record"

GIVEN f IS A `Forged Document Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the manner of the use` f MEANS
    CONCAT "did ", (`joined with` " and " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's fraudulently) "fraudulently"), (`included if` (f's dishonestly) "dishonestly")))),
           " use as genuine a forged ", (`the kind of forged thing` f), ", to wit, ", f's `the document`,
           (IF f's `the use` EQUALS "" THEN "" ELSE CONCAT ", by ", f's `the use`),
           ", which you ",
           (IF f's `knows it to be a forged document or forged electronic record` THEN "knew" ELSE "had reason to believe"),
           " to be a forged ", (`the kind of forged thing` f)

@export Frame a charge under section 471 of the Penal Code 1871 (using as genuine a forged document or forged electronic record), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Forged Document Facts` @desc The forged document, what the accused knew of it, how he used it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 471` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "471" "using as genuine a forged document or forged electronic record"
        (CONCAT "in the same manner as if he had forged such document or electronic record: ", (`the punishment under s 471` f)'s words)
        (`offence under s 471` f)
        (`the manner of the use` f)
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's fraudulently OR f's dishonestly) "fraudulently or dishonestly"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `uses as genuine`) "uses as genuine"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `a document` OR f's `an electronic record`) "any document or electronic record"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `knows it to be a forged document or forged electronic record` OR f's `has reason to believe it to be a forged document or forged electronic record`) "which he knows or has reason to believe to be a forged document or forged electronic record")))

@export Frame a charge under section 474 of the Penal Code 1871 (having possession of a forged document or electronic record of a description in section 466 or 467, with intent to use it as genuine), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Forged Document Facts` @desc The forged document, what the accused knew of it and intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 474` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "474" "having possession of a forged document or electronic record, knowing it to be forged, with intent to use it as genuine"
        ((`the punishment under s 474` f)'s words)
        (`offence under s 474` f)
        (CONCAT "did have in your possession a forged ", (`the kind of forged thing` f), ", to wit, ", f's `the document`,
                ", knowing the same to be forged, and intending that the same shall fraudulently or dishonestly be used as genuine")
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `has in his possession`) "has in his possession"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `a document` OR f's `an electronic record`) "any document or electronic record"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `knows it to be a forged document or forged electronic record`) "knowing the same to be forged"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `intending that the same shall fraudulently or dishonestly be used as genuine`) "intending that the same shall fraudulently or dishonestly be used as genuine"),
            (`missing unless` (`the forged document is of a description mentioned in section 466` f OR `the forged document is of a description mentioned in section 467` f) "one of the descriptions mentioned in section 466 or section 467")))

§§ `Counterfeit seals - ss 472, 473`

GIVEN f IS A `Counterfeit Seal Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the manner of the counterfeit seal` f MEANS
    CONCAT "did ",
           (IF f's `makes or counterfeits any seal, plate or other instrument for making an impression`
            THEN "make or counterfeit"
            ELSE "have in your possession, knowing the same to be counterfeit,"),
           " a seal, plate or other instrument for making an impression, to wit, ", f's `the instrument`

GIVEN f IS A `Counterfeit Seal Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of a counterfeit seal offence not made out` f MEANS
    `missing unless` (f's `makes or counterfeits any seal, plate or other instrument for making an impression` OR (f's `has in his possession any such seal, plate or other instrument` AND f's `knowing the same to be counterfeit`))
        "makes or counterfeits any seal, plate or other instrument for making an impression, or has in his possession any such seal, plate or other instrument, knowing the same to be counterfeit"

@export Frame a charge under section 472 of the Penal Code 1871 (making or possessing a counterfeit seal, plate, etc., with intent to commit a forgery punishable under section 467), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Counterfeit Seal Facts` @desc The instrument, what the accused did with it, what he intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 472` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "472" "making or possessing a counterfeit seal, plate, etc., with intent to commit a forgery punishable under section 467"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 472`'s words)
        (`offence under s 472` f)
        (CONCAT (`the manner of the counterfeit seal` f), ", intending that the same shall be used for the purpose of committing a forgery which would be punishable under section 467 of the Penal Code 1871")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of a counterfeit seal offence not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `intending that it shall be used for committing a forgery punishable under section 467`) "intending that the same shall be used for the purpose of committing any forgery which would be punishable under section 467")))

@export Frame a charge under section 473 of the Penal Code 1871 (making or possessing a counterfeit seal, plate, etc., with intent to commit a forgery punishable otherwise), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Counterfeit Seal Facts` @desc The instrument, what the accused did with it, what he intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 473` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "473" "making or possessing a counterfeit seal, plate, etc., with intent to commit a forgery punishable otherwise"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 473`'s words)
        (`offence under s 473` f)
        (CONCAT (`the manner of the counterfeit seal` f), ", intending that the same shall be used for the purpose of committing a forgery which would be punishable under Chapter 18 of the Penal Code 1871")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of a counterfeit seal offence not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `intending that it shall be used for committing a forgery punishable under another section of this Chapter`) "intending that the same shall be used for the purpose of committing any forgery which would be punishable under any section of this Chapter other than section 467")))

§§ `Equipment for false instruments - ss 473A, 473B`

GIVEN f IS A `False Instrument Equipment Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the holding of the equipment` f MEANS
    IF   f's `makes it`
    THEN "did make"
    ELSE "did have in your custody or under your control"

GIVEN f IS A `False Instrument Equipment Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`missing the making or custody` f MEANS
    `missing unless` (f's `makes it` OR f's `has it in his custody or under his control`) "makes or has in his custody or under his control a machine or implement, or paper or other material"

@export Frame a charge under section 473A of the Penal Code 1871 (making or possessing equipment for making a false instrument), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `False Instrument Equipment Facts` @desc The equipment, what the accused did with it and knew of it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 473A` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "473A" "making or possessing equipment for making a false instrument"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 473A`'s words)
        (`offence under s 473A` f)
        (CONCAT (`the holding of the equipment` f), " a machine or implement, or paper or other material, to wit, ", f's `the equipment`,
                ", which to your knowledge is or has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of a false instrument")
        (concat (LIST (`missing the making or custody` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `to his knowledge it is or has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of any false instrument`) "which to his knowledge is or has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of any false instrument")))

@export Frame a charge under section 473B of the Penal Code 1871 (making or possessing equipment for making a false instrument with intent to induce prejudice), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `False Instrument Equipment Facts` @desc The equipment, what the accused did with it and intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 473B` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "473B" "making or possessing equipment for making a false instrument with intent to induce prejudice"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 473B`'s words)
        (`offence under s 473B` f)
        (CONCAT (`the holding of the equipment` f), " a machine or implement, or paper or other material, to wit, ", f's `the equipment`,
                ", which is or has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of an instrument, intending that a false instrument be made using it in order to induce another person to accept it as genuine, and by reason of so accepting it to do or not to do some act to that person's or any other person's prejudice")
        (concat (LIST (`missing the making or custody` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `it is or has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of any instrument`) "which is or has been specifically designed or adapted for the making of any instrument"),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `intends that he or another person makes a false instrument using it in order to induce another person to accept it as genuine`) "intends that he or another person makes a false instrument using it in order to induce another person to accept it as genuine"),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `intends that by reason of so accepting it, that person does or does not do some act to his or any other person's prejudice`) "intends that by reason of so accepting it, that person does or does not do some act to his or any other person's prejudice")))

§§ `Counterfeit authenticating marks - ss 475, 476`

GIVEN f IS A `Counterfeit Mark Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the manner of the counterfeit mark` f MEANS
    CONCAT (IF f's `counterfeits upon or in the substance of any material any device or mark used for the purpose of authenticating a document`
            THEN "did counterfeit upon or in the substance of material a device or mark used for the purpose of authenticating documents, to wit, "
            ELSE "did have in your possession material upon or in the substance of which a device or mark used for the purpose of authenticating documents had been counterfeited, to wit, "),
           f's `the material`,
           ", intending that such device or mark shall be used for the purpose of giving the appearance of authenticity to any document then forged or thereafter to be forged on such material"

GIVEN f IS A `Counterfeit Mark Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of a counterfeit mark offence not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `counterfeits upon or in the substance of any material any device or mark used for the purpose of authenticating a document` OR f's `has in his possession any material upon or in the substance of which any such device or mark has been counterfeited`)
            "counterfeits upon or in the substance of any material any device or mark used for authenticating a document, or has in his possession any such material"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `intending that the device or mark shall be used to give the appearance of authenticity to a document then forged or thereafter to be forged on the material`)
            "intending that such device or mark shall be used for the purpose of giving the appearance of authenticity to any document then forged or thereafter to be forged on such material"))

@export Frame a charge under section 475 of the Penal Code 1871 (counterfeiting a device or mark used for authenticating documents described in section 467, or possessing counterfeit marked material), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Counterfeit Mark Facts` @desc The material, the device or mark, what the accused intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 475` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "475" "counterfeiting a device or mark used for authenticating documents described in section 467, or possessing counterfeit marked material"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 475`'s words)
        (`offence under s 475` f)
        (`the manner of the counterfeit mark` f)
        (concat (LIST (`elements of a counterfeit mark offence not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `the device or mark is used for authenticating a document described in section 467`) "a device or mark used for the purpose of authenticating any document described in section 467")))

@export Frame a charge under section 476 of the Penal Code 1871 (counterfeiting a device or mark used for authenticating documents or electronic records other than those described in section 467, or possessing counterfeit marked material), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Counterfeit Mark Facts` @desc The material, the device or mark, what the accused intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 476` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "476" "counterfeiting a device or mark used for authenticating documents or electronic records other than those described in section 467, or possessing counterfeit marked material"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 476`'s words)
        (`offence under s 476` f)
        (`the manner of the counterfeit mark` f)
        (concat (LIST (`elements of a counterfeit mark offence not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `the device or mark is used for authenticating a document or electronic record other than those described in section 467`) "a device or mark used for the purpose of authenticating any document or electronic record other than the documents described in section 467")))

§§ `Destruction of a will or valuable security - s 477`

@export Frame a charge under section 477 of the Penal Code 1871 (fraudulent cancellation, destruction, etc., of a will), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Will or Security Destruction Facts` @desc The document, what the accused did to it and with what intent, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 477` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "477" "fraudulent cancellation, destruction, etc., of a will"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 477`'s words)
        (`offence under s 477` f)
        (CONCAT "did ",
                (`joined with` ", " (concat (LIST
                    (`included if` (f's fraudulently) "fraudulently"),
                    (`included if` (f's dishonestly) "dishonestly"),
                    (`included if` (f's `with intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person`) "with intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person")))),
                " ", f's `the act`, " a document which is or purports to be ",
                (`joined with` " and " (concat (LIST
                    (`included if` (f's `is or purports to be a will`) "a will"),
                    (`included if` (f's `is or purports to be an authority to adopt a child`) "an authority to adopt a child"),
                    (`included if` (f's `is or purports to be a valuable security`) "a valuable security")))),
                ", to wit, ", f's `the document`)
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's fraudulently OR f's dishonestly OR f's `with intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person`) "fraudulently or dishonestly, or with intent to cause damage or injury to the public or to any person"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `cancels, destroys or defaces` OR f's `attempts to cancel, destroy or deface` OR f's secretes OR f's `attempts to secrete` OR f's `commits mischief in respect to such document`) "cancels, destroys, or defaces, or attempts to, or secretes, or attempts to, or commits mischief in respect to such document"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `is or purports to be a will` OR f's `is or purports to be an authority to adopt a child` OR f's `is or purports to be a valuable security`) "any document which is or purports to be a will, or an authority to adopt a child, or any valuable security")))

§§ `Falsification of accounts - s 477A`

-- Explanation 1: "a general intent to defraud", with no person or sum named.
GIVEN f IS A `Falsification of Accounts Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of falsification of accounts not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `being a clerk, officer or servant` OR f's `employed or acting in the capacity of a clerk, officer or servant`) "being a clerk, officer or servant, or employed or acting in the capacity of a clerk, officer or servant"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `acts intentionally`) "intentionally"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `with intent to defraud`) "with intent to defraud"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `destroys, alters, conceals, mutilates or falsifies` OR f's `makes or abets the making of any false entry in` OR f's `omits or alters or abets the omission or alteration of any material particular from or in`)
            "destroys, alters, conceals, mutilates or falsifies, or makes or abets the making of any false entry in, or omits or alters or abets the omission or alteration of any material particular from or in"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `any book, electronic record, paper, writing, valuable security or account or a set thereof`) "any book, electronic record, paper, writing, valuable security or account or a set thereof"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `belongs to or is in the possession of his employer` OR f's `has been received by him for or on behalf of his employer`) "which belongs to or is in the possession of his employer, or has been received by him for or on behalf of his employer"))

@export Frame a charge under section 477A of the Penal Code 1871 (falsification of accounts), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Falsification of Accounts Facts` @desc The accused's position, what he did to his employer's records and with what intent, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 477A` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "477A" "falsification of accounts"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 477A`'s words)
        (`offence under s 477A` f)
        (CONCAT "being ", f's `the capacity`, ", did intentionally and with intent to defraud ", f's `the falsification`)
        (`elements of falsification of accounts not made out` f)
